From: T0biii <5702338+T0biii@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:51:35 +0100
Subject: patches: openwrt: rockchip: wait after SD card power-off
 on NanoPi R2S

Set power-off-delay-us to one second in the NanoPi R2S device tree. A
UHS SD card is otherwise probably still in 1.8V signalling when the SoC
is reset, so that the boot ROM and U-Boot cannot read it and the board
hangs after a reboot or sysupgrade until the power is cycled. The cause
is not confirmed. This keeps the UHS modes of the card enabled.

Signed-off-by: T0biii <5702338+T0biii@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 ...opi-r2s-wait-after-SD-card-power-off.patch | 55 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 55 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 patches/openwrt/0033-rockchip-nanopi-r2s-wait-after-SD-card-power-off.patch

diff --git a/patches/openwrt/0033-rockchip-nanopi-r2s-wait-after-SD-card-power-off.patch b/patches/openwrt/0033-rockchip-nanopi-r2s-wait-after-SD-card-power-off.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5b93581
--- /dev/null
+++ b/patches/openwrt/0033-rockchip-nanopi-r2s-wait-after-SD-card-power-off.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+From 82281cabe5f08ac74e5c2e8b4b0b8e61337d3acd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: T0biii <5702338+T0biii@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:51:34 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 2/2] rockchip: nanopi-r2s: wait after SD card power-off
+
+Set power-off-delay-us to one second in the NanoPi R2S device tree so
+that the SD card can discharge before the SoC is reset. This is meant to
+fix the hang after a reboot or sysupgrade without disabling UHS.
+
+Signed-off-by: T0biii <5702338+T0biii@users.noreply.github.com>
+---
+ ...opi-r2s-wait-after-SD-card-power-off.patch | 34 +++++++++++++++++++
+ 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)
+ create mode 100644 target/linux/rockchip/patches-6.12/140-arm64-dts-rockchip-nanopi-r2s-wait-after-SD-card-power-off.patch
+
+diff --git a/target/linux/rockchip/patches-6.12/140-arm64-dts-rockchip-nanopi-r2s-wait-after-SD-card-power-off.patch b/target/linux/rockchip/patches-6.12/140-arm64-dts-rockchip-nanopi-r2s-wait-after-SD-card-power-off.patch
+new file mode 100644
+index 0000000..b00ddcf
+--- /dev/null
++++ b/target/linux/rockchip/patches-6.12/140-arm64-dts-rockchip-nanopi-r2s-wait-after-SD-card-power-off.patch
+@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
++From: T0biii <5702338+T0biii@users.noreply.github.com>
++Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
++Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: nanopi-r2s: wait after SD card
++ power-off
++
++On the NanoPi R2S a reboot or sysupgrade often leaves the board hanging
++until the power is removed. After the reboot only the SYS LED lights up
++and the board does not answer on the network.
++
++The cause is not confirmed. The likely explanation is that the SD card
++is still in 1.8V signalling when the SoC is reset. The RK3328 boot ROM
++and U-Boot talk to the card at 3.3V and cannot read it.
++
++The core waits only 1 ms after it has switched the card supply off.
++Set power-off-delay-us to one second so that the card can discharge
++before the SoC is reset. This keeps the UHS modes of the card enabled.
++
++Signed-off-by: T0biii <5702338+T0biii@users.noreply.github.com>
++---
++ arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2s.dts | 1 +
++ 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
++
++diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2s.dts
++index a4399da..ede6031 100644
++--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2s.dts
+++++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2s.dts
++@@ -352,6 +352,7 @@
++ 	disable-wp;
++ 	pinctrl-0 = <&sdmmc0_clk>, <&sdmmc0_cmd>, <&sdmmc0_dectn>, <&sdmmc0_bus4>;
++ 	pinctrl-names = "default";
+++	power-off-delay-us = <1000000>;
++ 	sd-uhs-sdr12;
++ 	sd-uhs-sdr25;
++ 	sd-uhs-sdr50;
